MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=14
DESCRIPTION=DevOps multi-agent team skill as an MCP server. .cursor/skills/devops-multi-agent-team/mcp/server.mjs is a dependency-free Node stdio MCP server, registered for the repo in .mcp.json as devops-multi-agent-team. It serves the skill (prompt devops, resource devops://skill), its references (devops://reference/<name>), the DevOps agent prompts (.cursor/agents/devops-*.md) and the slash commands (.cursor/commands/*.md) as prompts and resources, read from disk on each request so the Markdown stays the source of truth. Tools: list_docs, read_doc (catalog names only, no caller-built paths), mint_seat_id (role-identity.md seat id: 3 random bytes, rejected and re-minted while the id appears in any file name or content under .cursor/thoughts) and validate_push_json (push-json.md keys, seat ids, qa rows, hunks, delta, and that "to" is not an author; file reads limited to push-*.json in .cursor/thoughts/non-finalized). SKILL.md documents the server; role-identity.md names mint_seat_id as the MCP form of the one seat-id generator; push-json.md states the per-file {hunks, delta} shape. New /devops <goal> command starts the team as Orchestrator: .cursor/commands/devops.md (Cursor), with .claude/commands/devops.md a symlink to it (Claude Code); it loads the skill through the MCP read_doc tool or SKILL.md, and the server does not serve it as a second prompt. node --test .cursor/skills/devops-multi-agent-team/mcp/server.test.mjs covers the catalog, path rejection, seat ids, Push JSON checks and a stdio round trip.
